{"name":"Terrarium","hex":"#5f6d5c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"terrarium","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An enclosure wherein small animals are displayed, usually with some plants, in a naturalistic setting.","A partially enclosed glass container for displaying plants, especially plants that need high humidity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrarium"}],"entries":[{"title":"Terrarium","blocks":[{"text":"A terrarium is a glass container containing soil and plants in an environment different from the surroundings. It is usually a sealable container that can be opened for maintenance or to access the plants inside; however, terraria can also be open to the atmosphere. Terraria are often kept as ornamental items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Regenwaldterrarium.jpg/330px-Regenwaldterrarium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terrarium","wikidata":"Q1131243"},{"title":"Terrarium (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Terrarium is a 1985 science fiction novel by American writer and essayist Scott Russell Sanders, published by Tor."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/37/Terrarium_%28Scott_Russell_Sanders_book%29_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terrarium_(novel)","wikidata":"Q7703308"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b5/Ward%27scher_Kasten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b5/Ward%27scher_Kasten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"A drawing of a Wardian case","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWard'scher_Kasten.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/OpenTe